This repository contains a selected subset of the upstream source,
focused on Linux PCI/PCIe driver support.

Generated build artifacts, obsolete Big Kernel Lock implementation,
and unrelated operating system drivers have been excluded.

Modernization
-------------

The Linux modernization includes changes to kernel API compatibility,
PCI device lifecycle management, memory-mapped I/O handling,
character device management, and hardware module health validation.

The modernization was developed and tested using physical Quantis
hardware running Debian GNU/Linux 12 with a Linux 6.1 kernel.

New modifications and project-specific supporting code are
distributed under GPL-2.0-only.

Project maintainer: Seric <seric@seric.com>

Development included assistance from OpenAI ChatGPT. Hardware testing,
deployment, and operational validation were performed by the project
maintainer.

